client recieves empty SOAP response message when used as a client of gsoap server (https), some responses from server are considered by axis2 as empty. tcpdump shoes that there is actually a response. This problem seems to occurs when sending lot of SOAP requests in a short amount of time. This problem doesn't occurs in axis2-1.3 version (so I roll back to 1.3) traces are as follows : [ad90cssm@ssmsce2 logs]$ grep "14:29:11,863" obaossm-DebugFull.log.1.1429 2016-02-04 14:29:11,863 [574fad53-1566-44ab-a664-ac7f2d3293ed] DEBUG httpclient.wire.header - << "HTTP/1.1 200 OK[][
]" 2016-02-04 14:29:11,863 [574fad53-1566-44ab-a664-ac7f2d3293ed] DEBUG httpclient.wire.header - << "Server: gSOAP/2.7[][
]" 2016-02-04 14:29:11,863 [574fad53-1566-44ab-a664-ac7f2d3293ed] DEBUG httpclient.wire.header - << "Content-Type: text/xml; charset=utf-8[][
]" 2016-02-04 14:29:11,863 [574fad53-1566-44ab-a664-ac7f2d3293ed] DEBUG httpclient.wire.header - << "Content-Length: 2180[][
]" 2016-02-04 14:29:11,863 [574fad53-1566-44ab-a664-ac7f2d3293ed] DEBUG httpclient.wire.header - << "Connection: close[][
]" 2016-02-04 14:29:11,863 [574fad53-1566-44ab-a664-ac7f2d3293ed] DEBUG httpclient.wire.header - << "[][
]" 2016-02-04 14:29:11,863 [574fad53-1566-44ab-a664-ac7f2d3293ed] ERROR obao.ssm.communication.protocol.ProtocolOutPollerV114 - Connection error for suppressEquipments at endpoint : null Couple of comments/questions: Why is this issue labelled/flagged with "patch"? Where is the patch? Logs from a 1ms time window are not useful. Logs from application code (obao.ssm.communication.protocol.ProtocolOutPollerV114 in this case) are not useful unless they show the exception received from Axis2. Experience shows that this type of issue is often caused by misconfigured clients. You should add the relevant code snippet. Bug reports are more likely to receive attention if the issue is reproducible with the latest release (1.7.0 in this case). code snippet : // Use factory to create a RPCServiceClient instance RPCServiceClient serviceClient = _rpcClientFactory.getInstance(); Options options = serviceClient.getOptions(); // Set the end point destination EndpointReference targetEPR = new EndpointReference(endPoint); options.setTo(targetEPR); options.setProperty(org.apache.axis2.Constants.Configuration.CHARACTER_SET_ENCODING, "ISO-8859-1"); // set the timeout value (be careful for the change from second to // milli second. options.setTimeOutInMilliSeconds(Integer.parseInt(timeout) * 1000L); //Setting socket timeout value options.setProperty(HTTPConstants.SO_TIMEOUT, Integer.parseInt(timeout)* 1000); //Setting connection timeout value options.setProperty(HTTPConstants.CONNECTION_TIMEOUT, Integer.parseInt(timeout)* 1000); // try to cleanup the port after the sending options.setCallTransportCleanup(true); mc.setEnvelope(env); mepClient = serviceClient .createClient(ServiceClient.ANON_OUT_IN_OP); mepClient.addMessageContext(mc); .... // sending message try { mepClient.execute(true); } catch (AxisFault e) { log.error(CONNECTION_ERROR_FOR + messageName + AT_ENDPOINT + endPoint + COLON_2 + e.getMessage()); throw (e); } catch (Exception e) { log.error(CONNECTION_ERROR_FOR + messageName + AT_ENDPOINT + endPoint + COLON_2 + e.getMessage()); throw new AxisFault (e.getMessage()); } axis2.xml full content true false false false true 4000 false true --> true 30000 false false admin axis2 service --> modules --> axis2 --> services --> rest --> false false --> --> myhost.com --> false --> --> 60080 --> My-Server/1.1 --> 10000 --> false --> 50 --> 100 --> 240000 --> MILLISECONDS --> HTTP/1.1 chunked true --> HTTP/1.1 chunked --> --> N/A --> --> true multicast wso2.carbon.domain true 10 228.0.0.4 45564 500 3000 127.0.0.1 127.0.0.1 4000 true true 127.0.0.1 4000 127.0.0.1 4001 Hi Andreas, My answers: -patch: no patch, I'm just not able to fill the form -log for 1ms time: that all axis log I have when receiving soap response -code snippet: added with also full axis2.xml content -latest release: My application has just moved to 1.6.2 /1.6.4 (end of 2015)... regards The logs show this entry: So the code in ProtocolOutPollerV114 received an exception or an unexpected result from Axis2. In the first case, you should show the exception that is received. In the second case you should explain which Axis2 method is returning an unexpected result.

