]" 1516 [main] DEBUG httpclient.wire.content - >> " Hello World! " >>>>> 1985 [main] DEBUG httpclient.wire.header - Hello World! " >>>>> >>>>> public static EchoResponse parse(javax.xml.stream.XMLStreamReader reader) throws java.lang.Exception{ EchoResponse object = new EchoResponse(); int event; try { while (!reader.isStartElement() && !reader.isEndElement()) reader.next(); while (!reader.isStartElement() && !reader.isEndElement()) reader.next(); if (reader.isStartElement() && new javax.xml.namespace.QName("urn:SampleConnector","EchoResponse").equals(reader.getName())){ object.setEchoResponse(EchoOut.Factory.parse(reader)); } // End of if for expected property start element else{ // A start element we are not expecting indicates an invalid parameter was passed --->>>>>>>> throw new java.lang.RuntimeException("Unexpected subelement " + reader.getLocalName()); >>>>> Your WSDL has an rpc encoded binding! Axis2 does not support rpc/encoded bindings yet! > Your WSDL has an rpc encoded binding! Axis2 does not support rpc/encoded bindings yet! Can you tell me when you expect that to be available?? Thanks. Two things: 1. If the WSDL is rpc/encoded then Axis2 should *definitely* print a clear and early warning that we don't support this type of WSDL and generate NO code. 2. The Axis2 team is probably going to have to fully support rpc/encoded services as a client. Marking this as a blocker. We *Need* to inform the user that we don't support rpc/encoded during codegen. thanks, dims I think the issu is fixed in 1.1 , can you please check and confirm. pls resolve the isuee if it is fixed in the code base I put a proper error message to display when using encoding type wsdls.

